+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`priceOrder` in `src/pricing.ts` computes the percentage coupon on `grossTotal` rather than the sum of the lines after volume discounts. `Coupons.redeemable` in `src/coupons.ts` rejects `date >= validUntil`, excluding the last day. `src/tax.ts` `shippingVat` applies 22% to shipping and feeds the total, receipt and invoice summary.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Fix the coupon base and last-day check so the code matches the README.
+- Remove VAT on shipping and update the README to state the new rule.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Touching VAT on goods, shipping tiers, or the discount cap; migrating existing orders.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Coupon base: pass `sum(afterVolume)` to `couponDiscount` (still using `percentOf` from `src/money.ts`, integer cents). The cap keeps using gross. A fixed coupon is already capped by its base, which now is the post-volume subtotal, matching the README.
+- Last day: change the check to `compareDates(date, coupon.validUntil) > 0`.
+- Shipping VAT: delete `shippingVat` and `Totals.shippingVatCents`, rather than leaving a field that is always 0, so no stale 22% logic remains. Total = goods + shipping + vat. Receipt drops the "VAT on shipping" row. Invoice summary adds shipping at rate 0 with 0 VAT so the invoice total still equals the order total.
+- README is updated in the same change (VAT section), as it is the source of truth.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Removing `shippingVatCents` is a breaking change to the exported `Totals` type; accepted since the field would be meaningless.
+- Shipping merged into the 0% invoice row could mix with exempt goods at 0%; the row sums net and VAT so the summary stays correct.
+- VAT-free shipping may not be compliant for every case; flagged as out of scope in the proposal.
