+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Three reports on order pricing:
+
+1. Finance: an order that combines a volume discount with a percentage coupon gets too much off. 12 notebooks at €5.00 with a 10% coupon come to €48.00 of goods; €48.60 is expected. The coupon percentage is taken on the gross amount (€60.00 → €6.00) instead of the subtotal after volume discounts (€54.00 → €5.40), which the README requires.
+2. Luca: coupon AUTUMN, advertised as valid until 2026-11-30, was refused as expired on 2026-11-30. The README says the last day is included; the code rejects the last day itself.
+3. Anna: the receipt charges VAT on shipping (€1.08 on €4.90). The business decision is that delivery is a service and carries no VAT.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Percentage coupons are computed on the order subtotal after volume discounts (bug fix; README already correct).
+- A coupon is redeemable on its last valid day (bug fix; README already correct).
+- **Rule change**: shipping carries no VAT. The README's VAT rules are updated: the line "Shipping is subject to VAT at the standard rate (22%), shown on its own line of the receipt" is replaced, and the order total becomes goods + shipping + VAT on goods. The receipt drops its "VAT on shipping" line, and the invoice VAT summary shows shipping at 0%.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `coupons`: coupon discount base and validity period (first and last day included).
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `vat`: adds the requirement that shipping carries no VAT and the order total excludes shipping VAT.
+
+## README business rules affected
+
+- Discounts: "Coupons … applies to the order's subtotal after volume discounts" and "valid from its first day to its last day, both included" — unchanged, code is brought in line.
+- VAT: "Shipping is subject to VAT at the standard rate (22%)…" and "The order total is goods + shipping + VAT on goods + VAT on shipping" — **changed** (README update included).
+- Money, Shipping (free from €50.00, weight tiers): unchanged.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Code: `src/pricing.ts`, `src/coupons.ts`, `src/tax.ts`, `src/receipt.ts`, `src/invoices.ts`; the `Totals.shippingVatCents` field is removed (public type via `src/index.ts`).
+- Tests: `test/orders.test.ts`, `test/coupons.test.ts`.
+- Docs: `README.md` VAT section.
+- Behaviour change visible to customers: totals of every order with paid shipping fall by 22% of the shipping cost.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Changing VAT on goods, shipping tiers, the free-shipping threshold or the 50% discount cap.
+- Re-pricing, re-receipting or re-invoicing orders already placed or invoiced.
+- Whether tax law permits VAT-free shipping for particular products or destinations; this change implements the stated business decision only.
+- Fixed-amount coupons, which already take at most the subtotal after volume discounts.
